{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias in rising markets: when the last 10–20 days show a clear uptrend, add an upward level shift to the whole path (model underestimates by ~+1 to +4 €/t, largest around days 5–20).",
    "Underreacts to upside momentum (lag): if recent returns are strongly positive, steepen the first half of the forecast (days 1–15) because the model’s slope is too flat versus realized.",
    "Peak timing/shape error: the model tends to peak too early and too low; delay the peak slightly and increase peak amplitude (especially around days 8–18).",
    "Late-horizon overprediction after a rally: beyond ~day 20 the model often stays too high while realized prices mean-revert; apply stronger downward drift/mean reversion in days 20–30.",
    "Asymmetric regime behavior: apply larger positive corrections in bullish regimes than negative corrections in bearish/mean-reverting regimes (errors are dominated by missing upside rather than downside)."
  ]
}
